course: dictionary
lesson: 15347
title: Stiff words and what they ask for
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A solicitation is a formal word for a request. Someone makes a solicitation when they ask you for money, help, business or support. «The charity sent a solicitation asking for donations for the flood victims.» The words sent, donations and flood victims are context clues: someone is asking for something.
explain: Signs use this word too. «The notice on the gate said: No solicitation.» Read the words around it. A sign like that means salespeople and collectors must not knock or ask people to buy or give. Always ask: what would fit here? Then try a simpler word, like request, in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
explain: Words like solicitation are stiff and formal. You will meet them in letters, notices, law and exam texts. You do not need to know every word to understand a text, so read the clues around the word, make a guess, and check it in a dictionary if you are still unsure.
fact: Solicitation is a noun: a solicitation, solicitations.
fact: Solicitation means a request asking someone for money, help, business or support.
fact: A solicitation for donations is a request from a charity.
fact: «No solicitation» on a sign means salespeople and collectors must not knock or ask.
fact: In law, solicitation is the crime of asking or urging someone to do something illegal.
exercise: «The charity sent a solicitation asking for donations for the flood victims.» What is a solicitation here? | A kind of boat | *A request for money or help | A flood of water | A shiny new coat
exercise: A sign on the gate says «No solicitation». What must salespeople not do? | *Knock or ask people to buy or give | Ask the dog for help | Walk past the gate | Leave a gift at the gate
exercise: «The club made a solicitation for new members and volunteers.» Find and copy the word that names a request for help. | club | *solicitation | members | volunteers
test: The school sent a solicitation letter asking parents for support with the summer fair. What is a solicitation letter? | A letter that says thank you for a gift | *A letter asking for money, help or support | A letter written in code | A letter from the post office
test: In law, what does solicitation mean? | Cleaning up a park | *Urging someone to do something illegal | Being happy with a deal | Giving a present to a friend
exam: «The notice on the gate said: No solicitation.» Why must the man selling brushes leave? | He wanted to see the sea | *Because the sign says salespeople must not ask people to buy | He had sold every brush he carried | He was given a gift by the owner
